        stem='In a simple polystyrene cup calorimeter, 50.0 cm3 of 1.00 mol dm^-3 HCl(aq) is mixed with 50.0 cm3 of 1.00 mol dm^-3 NaOH(aq). The temperature of the solution rises by 6.5 °C.\n[Specific heat capacity of solution = 4.18 J g^-1 K^-1; density of solution = 1.00 g cm^-3]\n\nWhat is the quantity of thermal energy (q) released in this experiment?',
        options=['A: 1359 J (1.36 kJ)', 'B: 5434 J (5.43 kJ)', 'C: 680 J (0.68 kJ)', 'D: 2717 J (2.72 kJ)'],
        correct_answer='D',
        explanation='Option D is correct. Total volume of reacting solution = 50.0 + 50.0 = 100.0 cm3. Mass of solution m = volume x density = 100.0 cm3 x 1.00 g cm^-3 = 100.0 g. Thermal energy released: q = m x c x Delta T = 100.0 g x 4.18 J g^-1 K^-1 x 6.5 K = 2717 J = 2.717 kJ.',
